vaevictis-aurora (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security hardening: song titles and artists read from the files are
    escaped before they are shown or sent to the desktop notification, so a
    file's tags can never inject formatting or links.
  * The duration fallback (ffprobe) always receives an absolute path.

 -- linuxtuts-website <292920559+linuxtuts-website@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200

vaevictis-aurora (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The spectrum now analyses the audio that is playing (it used random
    numbers before). It is a full-width strip above the player bar, with a
    frequency read-out when you hover a bar.
  * Sharper text: real bold instead of weight 600, better contrast.
  * QT_QPA_PLATFORM can be set from the shell (for example xcb) to test X11.
  * First release as a .deb: it replaces a hand-copied /usr/local/bin/aurora.

 -- linuxtuts-website <292920559+linuxtuts-website@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0200
